base, `reloadCurrentDirectory` is public and called from multiple places like the context menu and extraction callbacks, while `loadDirectory` is private. The cleanest solution is to save the scroll position before `loadPath` gets called and restore it right after setting the adapter. I need to make `fileListView` accessible so I can read and restore its scroll state. Writing the scroll position restoration code... I need to preserve the scroll position when reloading the directory by capturing the first visible item position and offset before the reload, then restoring it afterward in the `loadDirectory` method.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
